    "path": "poems/a-poem-for-my-love-jasper-faye-szimanski.json",
    "schema_version": "1.0",
    "work_type": "poem",
    "title": "A poem for my love Jasper Faye Szimanski",
    "subtitle": null,
    "author": "William Saville",
    "date_written": "January 6, 2024",
    "date_revised": null,
    "content": "When their smile is like sunshine,\nWhen your sky is full of storms,\nWhen they whisper words of love,\nMy ice wall slowly warms.\nProtected my heart from endless trauma,\nWith these walls of ice I built,\nInstead of breaking my walls down,\nThey warm them instead of guilt.\nEach day we live on halted breath,\nHand in hand we take the days\nWaiting for the other shoe to drop,\nTaking solace in each other's gaze.\nTraumas are talked about,\nRather than avoided or buried,\nMaking us better partners,\nKnowing each other's hearts are carried.\nPave the road ahead of us,\nWith each moment and heartbeat,\nMore precious than diamonds or gold,\nNo decadent dessert could be as sweet.\nSo my love and my partner,\nThey are the fire inside me,\nPushing me to do more than survive,\nI want to be more than happy.\nWith them I can have a life,\nWorth living hand in hand\nI can thrive in their embrace,\nNo matter what we withstand."
